# lint-staged runs per workspace package; add a line here when a package joins.
#
# Hook-covered, one line each below: apps/website, apps/outlook-addon,
# apps/tb-addon and packages/pg-js — the four that are edited by hand every day,
# where formatting on commit keeps style churn out of the next diff.
#
# CI-covered only: examples/pg-manual, examples/pg-node and examples/pg-sveltekit.
# All three declare `lint` and the Node examples job in examples.yml runs it on
# every PR, so an unformatted example still cannot merge. The two lists differ on
# cost, not on principle: a line here is paid on every commit in the repo, and the
# examples are touched a few times a year. pg-sveltekit has been in that shape
# since the import; #269 put the other two there with it.
#
# A package needs its own prettier config before it can be listed here, and a
# config at the REPO ROOT is not the way to give it one: prettier resolves config
# by walking up from each file and a package.json without a `prettier` key does
# not stop the search, so one root config silently becomes the style of every
# package that has none. See apps/tb-addon/CLAUDE.md.
#
# Each line runs with that package's directory as cwd, which is what makes the
# package's own prettier config and .prettierignore apply.
pnpm --filter postguard-website exec lint-staged
pnpm --filter postguard-outlook-addin exec lint-staged
pnpm --filter postguard-tb-addon exec lint-staged
pnpm --filter @e4a/pg-js exec lint-staged
